[38;5;231m⏺[39m I read through the settings page. [38;5;153mpublic/settings.html[39m holds 12 fields in one flex column, and they fall into four
  groups:

  - [1mProfile:[0m display name, email, avatar URL
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor auth, session timeout, API token

  How to lay those groups out is easier to judge by looking, so I've opened a browser tab with sketches:
  [94m]8;id=k5nwtz;http://localhost:49462/?key=c20d236d88e523c0e27870ec7bc36802da0ff2e42285929a18365011e0a3b766\http://localhost:49462/?key=c20d236d88e523c0e27870ec7bc36802da0ff2e42285929a18365011e0a3b766[39m]8;;\ (this uses a lot of
  tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal).

  The tab shows three options:

  - [1mA. Stacked sections:[0m each group gets a heading, one after another on the same page, with one Save button. This is
    the smallest change.
  - [1mB. Card grid:[0m each group in its own card, two by two on wide screens. The page would need to be wider than its
    current 640px.
  - [1mC. Side nav / tabs:[0m only one group shows at a time. This needs JavaScript to switch between groups.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. It fixes the scanning problem without hiding any fields or changing how the form saves. The field names
  stay the same, so [38;5;153msettings.js[39m and the [38;5;153m/api/settings[39m request won't change.

  Do the four groups look right, and which layout do you want? You can click an option in the tab or answer here.

  The sketches are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the project. That folder isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet, so I'd add it there.

